-- title:
--   Finite flat closed subgroup with toric points is the toric lift
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a nonzero modulus $M$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`) whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$; let $\Lambda$ be level data for $p, M, H$ over $A$, consisting of a structure morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to \mathtt{base } p$ compatible with the generic point, a scheme over $\mathtt{base } p$ with a relative group law and dictionaries for its generic and special points, and let $O$ be a Néron object at $p$ for these data, with total space $O.G$, structure morphism $O.g$, relative group law $O.L$, bijection $O.\mathrm{pts}$ from $J_H(M) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the level-$H$ function field over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ onto the $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $O.G$ over the generic point, toric rank $t = O.\mathrm{toricRank}$ and toric lifts $O.\mathrm{toricLift}$. Fix $m > 0$ and a commutative ring $B$ carrying an $A$-Hopf algebra structure which is finite and flat as an $A$-module, together with a morphism $i$ from $\operatorname{Spec} B$ to the base change $O.G \times_{\mathtt{base } p} \operatorname{Spec} A$ lying over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $A \to B$. Assume: (i) $i$ is a closed immersion; (ii) for all $\chi, \chi'$ in `WithConv` of the $A$-algebra maps $B \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ and all $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, x', xx'$ of the base change over `barPt A`, if $x$, $x'$, $xx'$ are $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\chi$, of $\chi'$, of $\chi \cdot \chi'$ respectively followed by $i$, then $xx'$ is the product of $x$ and $x'$ under the base-changed group law $O.L$; (iii) an element $y$ of $J_H(M)$ lies in the subgroup $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$, generated by the toric points at level $m$, exactly when $O.\mathrm{pts}\,y$ is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of some $A$-algebra map $\chi \colon B \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ followed by $i$ followed by the first projection. The conclusion asserts the existence of an isomorphism $e$ of $A$-bialgebras from $B$ to the group algebra $A[(\mathbb{Z}/m)^{t}]$ such that, first, $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $e^{-1}$ followed by the toric lift at level $m$ equals $i$; and second, $e$ is compatible with towers: for every $m'>0$ with $m \mid m'$, every commutative ring $B'$ with an $A$-bialgebra structure and isomorphism $e' \colon B' \to A[(\mathbb{Z}/m')^{t}]$ of $A$-bialgebras, every $A$-algebra $D$ with a monomorphism $j$ from $\operatorname{Spec} D$ into $O.G \times_{\mathtt{base } p} \operatorname{Spec} A$, and all $A$-algebra maps $a \colon D \to B$, $a' \colon D \to B'$ such that $\operatorname{Spec} a$ followed by $j$ is $i$ and $\operatorname{Spec} a'$ followed by $j$ is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $(e')^{-1}$ followed by the toric lift at level $m'$, one has $e(a(z)) = e'(a'(z))$ pushed forward along the bialgebra map induced by the componentwise reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/m')^{t} \to (\mathbb{Z}/m)^{t}$, for all $z \in D$.
--
--   This is the rigidity statement that a finite flat closed subgroup scheme of the base-changed Néron object over the valuation ring $A$, whose $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-points are precisely the toric $m$-torsion points, must coincide with Grothendieck's toric lift $\mu_{m,A}^{t}$, with the identification of its coordinate ring with the group algebra $A[(\mathbb{Z}/m)^{t}]$ being compatible with reduction from level $m'$ to level $m$. It is used in the analysis of the toric part of the special fibre, notably by [`ModularCurve.exists_verschiebung_bialgEquiv_and_reducesToOne_and_tower_toricClosure_finitePart_jHNeronObjectAtP`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_verschiebung_bialgEquiv_and_reducesToOne_and_tower_toricClosure_finitePart_jHNeronObjectAtP), [`ModularCurve.nonempty_bialgEquiv_baseChange_residueField_torusQuotient_one_addMonoidAlgebra_of_finPtsWitness`](thm.html#ModularCurve.nonempty_bialgEquiv_baseChange_residueField_torusQuotient_one_addMonoidAlgebra_of_finPtsWitness) and [`ModularCurve.specMap_cokernel_comp_levelBaseChange_comp_abq_eq_one_of_finPtsWitness`](thm.html#ModularCurve.specMap_cokernel_comp_levelBaseChange_comp_abq_eq_one_of_finPtsWitness).
